int-0002  Zero-ceremony operation — one binary, no server, no  active 2026-07-29
          daemon
            no JSON API layer, no client runtime, no service to operate
└─ dec-0012  Surfaces are server-rendered Go templates and   accepted 2026-07-30
             static output — no SPA, no dira-operated host
   ├─ ✗ An embedded static SPA served from the binary, as design.md §9
   │    originally specified
   │    Three problems, and the first is fatal to the growth engine. The
   │    rendered decision pages are the long-tail SEO surface named in
   │    .agents/product-marketing.md §7 channel 4 — "every rendered decision
   │    page is a page answering why did project X choose Y" — and client-side
   │    rendering makes them uncrawlable, so the SPA actively undercuts
   │    dec-0010. Second, the three built screens in docs/design/screens/
   │    contain zero JavaScript, so an SPA is a runtime added for nothing
   │    already designed. Third, on localhost the data is already in-process, so
   │    a JSON API layer exists only to serialise to yourself.
   │    revisit if  a surface appears that genuinely needs client-side state — a
   │                graph explorer with live filtering, not a document view
   ├─ ✗ A hosted renderer at dira.sire.run
   │    design.md §9 sketches this as Tier 3 "much later", and dec-0005 already
   │    rejected dira-operated infrastructure for sync on ops-burden grounds —
   │    no ops, no on-call, no security surface for a solo maintainer already
   │    carrying kazi. That reasoning transfers intact to rendering. It would
   │    also make cst-0004 a promise that has to be kept rather than a property
   │    of the architecture.
   │    revisit if  teams pull for zero-setup shared rendering, per dec-0007's
   │                team tier
   └─ ✗ Ship both — static output now, hosted later
        Designing two serving paths before either is validated. The static path
        is strictly more constrained, so it can be extended into a hosted one
        later without rework; the reverse is not true.

edges
  informs      cst-0004  dira never requires a network service, an account, or a
